    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe fail-fast watcher added in #45053 aborts `TestPerturbRaiseMha` when its intentionally corrupted KV cache makes the server exit. The canary correctly reports `verify_real_kv_hash`, but the watcher exits the test runner before it can assert the captured violation. This caused [this CI failure](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39220756454/job/117959479275) on #44623.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `CustomTestCase.expect_server_exit`, defaulting to false. Opted-in tests run their assertions without a fail-fast watcher or retries against a terminated server.\n- Opt in only the canary raise-mode fault-injection test; preserve its violation assertions.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Pre-commit checks passed for the changed Python files.\n- Use the existing `test/registered/kv_canary/test_self_e2e_perturb_raise.py` as the regression test: it must complete its `verify_real_kv_hash` violation assertions after the intentional server exit. It remains registered for CUDA and AMD CI.\n- Targeted GPU rerun passed on `1-gpu-5090` at commit `f5333ca417c`: [workflow run](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39257555152). The existing canary test triggered the expected `verify_real_kv_hash` violation and completed successfully: `Ran 1 test in 51.741s`, `OK`.\n\nNo model execution or inference performance changes.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39256154023](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39256154023)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39256153890](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39256153890)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39256154039](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39256154039)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n",
